    "body": "Okay, I've confirmed that this happens in bash 5.1.16 as well, it just wasn't an issue on unix platforms because those used tarfiles instead of zipfiles.\r\n\r\nHonestly, I'm going to propose that we just add `-o` (overwrite without prompting) to the flags used for `unzip`. This already matches the behavior of `tar` (clobber without prompting) and lets us get around the incredibly nasty problem of trying to reset `stdin` to terminal before forking a child.",
